","rust","serverless"],"visibility":"public","forks":849,"open_issues":509,"watchers":20439,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neondatabase/neon/pulls/1791","html_url":"https://github.com/neondatabase/neon/pull/1791","diff_url":"https://github.com/neondatabase/neon/pull/1791.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/neondatabase/neon/pull/1791.patch","merged_at":"2022-05-25T15:13:03Z"},"body":"By default, etcd makes a huge 10 GB mmap() allocation when it starts up.\r\nIt doesn't actually use that much memory, it's just address space, but\r\nit caused me grief when I tried to use 'rr' to debug a python test run.\r\nApparently, when you replay the 'rr' trace, it does allocate memory for\r\nall that address space.\r\n\r\nThe size of the initial mmap depends on the --quota-backend-bytes setting.\r\nOur etcd clusters are very small, so let's set --quota-backend-bytes to\r\nkeep the virtual memory size small, to make debugging with 'rr' easier.\r\n\r\nSee https://github.com/etcd-io/etcd/issues/7910 and\r\nhttps://github.com/etcd-io/etcd/commit/5e4b0081065925ab9d04009cd4fb559c4cceb304","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neondatabase/neon/issues/1791/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neondatabase/neon/issues/1791/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":6677927034,"node_id":"REFE_lADOAKtHts4Nl7kwzwAAAAGOCRR6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/etcd-io/etcd/issues/events/6677927034","actor":{"login":"hlinnaka","id":191602,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTYwMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191602?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hlinnaka","html_url":"https://github.com/hlinnaka","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/